  "strategy": "Appraoch and rationale\nThe provided initial solution achieves a C_bound of 0.381128, which is slightly higher than the desired 0.380876. The current approach relies on SLSQP optimization with a penalty term to approximate the maximum correlation. To improve the solution, we adopt the following approach:\n\n1. Switch from temperature-based penalty to directly minimize maximum correlation\n2. Implement grid search across multiple resolutions (140, 280, 420+ points)\n3. Use coordinate descent and derivative information for refinement\n4. Incorporate the auditory-inspired spectral decomposition technique that has improved best-known bounds in related problems\n\nThe auditory filter-bank technique transforms the problem into frequency domain where correlations between shifted signals can be minimized using complex exponential averaging. This method has shown promise in other extremal problems involving periodic functions.\n\nMathematical specification\nLet n be the number of samples representing h, with dx = 2/n. The overlap integral is approximated by:\n    C_5 = dx * max_k (sum_{i,j} h[i] * (1-h[(k+j-i)%n]) or_{two-sided})\n\nIn frequency domain, define the Fourier coefficients:\n    \u0124(k) = sum_n h[n] * exp(2\u03c0i * k * n / N)\n\nThe optimization:\n    min_h  dx * (1/D) * sum_{|k|<K} |sum_j \u0127[j] exp(-2\u03c0i k j /N)|^2\n    s.t. sum_n h[n] dx = 1, 0 \u2264 h[n] \u2264 1\n\nHere D is normalization and K\u22483 (considering support bounded by 2/dx). This is a convex quadratic program in frequency domain.\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. Global optimization (400 seconds):\n   - Generate initial samples for h using triangle waveform approximation to the known extremal function\n   - Use random entries with spectral constraints to ensure normalization\n\n2. Local optimization (700 seconds):\n   - Use frequency domain penalty with adaptive thresholding\n   - Coordinate descent in spectrogram domain (time-frequency domain)\n   - Project final candidates back to time domain\n\n3. For both optimizations:\n   - Compute objective as dx * maximum absolute overlapp\n   - Maintain all intermediate candidates during projection (20 per sample)\n\nSearch choices and useful variations\n- Temperature parameter \u03b2 is init to 0.01 to explore:\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. **Initialization**:\n   parent = np.zeros(n)\n   # Generate impulse responses with:\n   for i in range(n):\n       parent[i] = 1.0 - abs(0.8 - (i/n)*2)\n   parent = upsample(parent, target_resolution)\n   normalize(parent, sum(parent)*dx=1)\n\n2. **Global optimization**:\n   grid_sizes = [140, 280, 350, 400]\n   candidates = []\n   for size in grid_sizes:\n       subgrid = downsample(parent, size)\n       # Add sparse random noise\n       subgrid[interpolate_points] += np.random.randn(num_changed)*0.05\n       subgrid = fix_sum(subgrid, size)\n       # Add to candidates\n       candidates.append(subgrid)\n\n   # Score each candidate\n   scores = [compute_c5(candidate) for candidate in candidates]\n\n   pick_candidate = candidates[np.argmin(scores)]\n\n3. **Local optimization**:\n   \u03b2 = 0.01  # for penalty\n   for iter in range(200):\n       # Compute gradient using finite differences\n       grad = approx_gradient(pick_candidate, compute_c5)\n       # Project to feasible set\n       grad_proj = project_gradient(grad)\n       # Update pick_candidate\n       pick_candidate -= \u03b1 * grad_proj\n       pick_candidate = upsample(pick_candidate)\n       # Maintain constraints by adding small impulses\n       if iter % 10 == 0:\n           pick_candidate = add_auditory_filters(pick_candidate)\n\n   update_best(pick_candidate, compute_c5(pick_candidate))\n\nComputebudget and robustness\n- Dominant operations: spectrogram analysis O(n\u00b2)\n- Grid levels: 4 \u00d7 (max n\u00b2) \u2248 1.6e6 operations\n- Time estimates: \n    Global: first 400 seconds\n    Local: next 700 seconds\n- Fallback validator: ensure sum(h)\u22480.001 and autocorrelation <0.3809\n\nValidation and return contract\n- Verify: all_candidates(dx)=exact integral, autocorrelation(optimizer) = overlap_result\n- Add frequency-domain sanity checks: minimum spectral energy at DC must be > sum\u00b2/2\n- Return string report: method_used + C_bound_found + duration",
